  "scope": "Bounded non-executable feedback for valid Fara navigation proposals with unsupported URL schemes",
  "status": {
    "implemented": true,
    "compiled": true,
    "tested": "16 distinct selected methods passed, no skips; unchanged real GitHub task failed its completion oracle",
    "accepted": "Decoder, local recovery and adjacent control regression scope only; autonomous task and production not accepted"
  },
  "changes": [
    "Decode syntactically valid unsupported schemes into a dedicated proposal carrying no executable URL. Relative/malformed/oversized/credential-bearing URLs and malformed tool calls still fail strictly.",
    "Validate current task/browser/page/login authority before retaining the rejected proposal and bounded tool error. Neither initial nor loaded-page recovery dispatches the rejected URL or rewrites it into a permitted URL.",
    "Allow three cumulative recovery opportunities per live session. A fourth unsupported navigation stores a terminal failure; replay cannot reset the budget or cause more proposals.",
    "Preserve the raw proposal and actual failure-bearing observation in bounded model history so the next action can use existing page reading or choose an ordinary supported destination."
  ],
  "findings": [
    "The new decoder/history test first failed with invalidResponse on the unmodified production implementation; its compiled red result is retained.",
    "Seven unsupported schemes decode to no executable URL and can be retained in model history. Blank and loaded actual WebKit workflows each reject three schemes, navigate only once to the allowed source, read it, complete and replay without effects.",
    "Repeated rejection stops after four proposals for blank and loaded pages. Six authority withdrawal variants cover paused control, a replacement owner and a revoked source for both the existing source-policy refusal and the new unsupported scheme.",
    "Eleven adjacent tests pass, including controlled login pause/Resume, initial and loaded observation cancellation, uncertain redirects, existing URL policy feedback, tooltip reading and extraction/history bounds.",
    "The real unchanged task reaches the correct release URL but times out without a terminal answer. Ten captured model replies select navigation, clicks, scrolling and browser Find; none requests an unsupported URL or the page reader in this trial. It therefore does not exercise live-model recovery or establish whole-task success.",
    "The task has a 100-second execution budget; the report elapsed time is 106.42 seconds including surrounding work/cleanup. At most one worker is observed in 883 samples, with zero after shutdown. The existing main-thread UI warning remains."
  ],
  "remainingWork": [
    "Resolve general browser tool selection using bounded reproducible diagnostics before another full live task; retain the independent version/date/link oracle. This trial gives no evidence to claim model recovery or increase the deadline.",
    "Qualify initial document readiness, without relying on model startup latency or weakening stale-page validation.",
    "Continue MCP-first native and browser coverage; qualify real-provider login, physical-phone controls, native/cross-app tasks, whole-Mac 12 GB resources/heat and production acceptance."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Production MCP priority, model selection, the 4 GiB worker cap, and the running installed application are unchanged.",
    "Successful local workflows use scripted proposals and extraction over real owned WebKit pages; they are not actual-model end-to-end acceptance.",
    "The public task uses the existing diagnostic HostSession composition, normal runtime/loader, explicit exchange observer and isolated journals.",
    "All four attempts are retained. No new network model download, model comparison, purchase, account sign-in or external communication was performed."
  ],
